  "notes": "Files read (both under E:/Projects/IDCOL 2.0/Loan Repayment Schedule (The Heart)/Hydron/): Hydron_Mini-Grid_ Loan_Restructured.xlsx and Hydron_Mini-Grid_2nd_Restructured_Feb'21.xlsx. Compared against the ORIGINAL (Hydron_Mini-Grid_ Loan.xlsx) and EX_DATA['HYDRON'] in frontend/lib/examples.ts to isolate exactly where each restructure diverges from the prior version, using both the \"Repayment Schedule\" sheet and the wider \"Hydron_Loan\" sheet (which carries the full, non-truncated installment series) in each workbook.\n\nEvent 1 (Hydron_Mini-Grid_ Loan_Restructured.xlsx): Classified as PREPAYMENT rather than RESTRUCTURE because the interest rate (6%), day-count (ACT/360), payment frequency (quarterly) and principal type (Level Principal) are all unchanged from the original — the only change is a single large lump-sum principal payment of BDT 14,731,306 on 2017-07-02 (vs. the originally scheduled installment of 541,841.47), which paid down the balance from 15,713,402.59 to 982,096.59. The loan then re-amortizes on the same level-principal cadence over the remaining 28 quarterly installments, closing to zero by 2024-06-30. No rate change, no tenor extension, no capitalization, no waiver found in this workbook (Disbursement/Summary/Accrual_Hydron sheets show no other adjustments).\n\nEvent 2 (Hydron_Mini-Grid_2nd_Restructured_Feb'21.xlsx): Classified as RESTRUCTURE. This file is identical to Event 1's post-prepayment schedule through 2020-01-01 (closing balance 631,347.81), then diverges: a 4-quarter moratorium runs 2020-03-30 through 2020-12-30 (principal payments = 0, unpaid interest capitalized quarterly into the opening balance each period — verified as closing = opening + interest for all 4 quarters), consistent with a COVID-19-era regulatory relief/moratorium (I inferred \"BB regulatory relief\" from context since this is a Bangladeshi NBFI and the timing/mechanics match the widely-documented 2020 BB moratorium circulars, but no explicit circular number is stated anywhere in the workbook, so I left regulatoryReference as a general description rather than fabricating a specific circular number — treat with some caution). Total interest capitalized over the moratorium = BDT 39,181.92, which matches exactly the workbook's own \"Total Interest Capitalized\" cell (Hydron_Loan!B52 = 39181.9220095442). After capitalization, the loan re-amortizes from 2021-03-31 onward with a new (lower, since balance increased slightly but tenor extended) level-principal installment of BDT 37,251.65 per quarter, running for 18 installments through 2025-06-30, closing to essentially zero (5.8e-11, floating point noise).\n\nBoth events use ACT/360 day-count with the stated 6% annual rate (verified interest = opening_balance * 0.06 * actual_days/360 reproduces the workbook's interest figures to full precision for sampled periods). Despite this clean derivability of interest, I used the override arrays (interest_payment_amounts / opening_balance_amounts / closing_balance_amounts) for both versions rather than relying on the engine's own date-generation logic, because the repayment dates are irregular (calendar-quarter-end dates that sometimes shift to the 1st/2nd of the following month, e.g. 2016-10-02, 2017-01-01, 2022-10-02, 2023-07-02) and a \"clean\" quarterly-interval generator might not reproduce the exact same date sequence — pinning to the workbook's actual row-by-row values, which were verified to close to zero (or ~1e-10, pure floating-point residue) at the end of each version's own life, guarantees fidelity per the task's stated preference for accuracy over derivational elegance.\n\nNo rate changes, no waived (forgiven) amounts, and no overdue-principal roll-in were found in either file — all \"overdue\" figures in the Summary sheets (e.g. Repayment overdue / Interest overdue columns) reflect timing differences in the summary's monthly view versus the quarterly schedule, not principal write-offs, and were not rolled into a new opening balance as an add-on (the moratorium capitalization already captures the only real balance-increasing adjustment).\n\nIgnored the ~$ Excel lock file per instructions (none was present for this borrower in any case — only the three real workbooks existed, one of which, Hydron_Mini-Grid_ Loan.xlsx, is the ORIGINAL already covered by EX_DATA and was used only as a diff baseline, not as a separate version entry)."
